"api":"openai.chat","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-6-luna","response_model":"openai/gpt-6-luna","response_id":"gen-1793273743-3gtCHFEsyilmqBPyG285"},"stop":"tool_use"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"toolresult","call":{"provider":"call_JsBkt1kuG3zHkX9gS67XM7yF"},"name":"search_world","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell was born on Orin and moved to Vesper at age six, where she grew up. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← UNRELATED_TO from Bren Vale (person) [ID: 3866be6c-f8eb-4158-8abb-a95e3ddc64b2] [Aliases: Captain]: Bren Vale captains the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock also call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild; he refuses to join because he distrusts Tal Ren's friends. He supports the toll on blue salt shipments imposed in 319 because its revenue will repair fishing piers. Nessa is his older sister and the Petrel's cook, not his employee on a formal wage.\n  - ← NAVIGATOR_FOR from Iven Marr (person) [ID: 1b66c764-9ef7-438c-afa7-22338885a61e]: Asha Pell's navigator and the only person who knows she has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates the Nightjar using tide charts, not magic.\n  - CAPTAINS → Nightjar (ship, courier ship) [ID: 36eac936-9ce0-4b27-9bf4-f77ae290dfa1]: A courier ship captained by Asha Pell. It carries blue salt from Orin to Vesper only between April and September.\n  - GREW_UP_IN → Vesper (city, port city) [ID: ccb13663-df18-4e63-b89c-006464a6cfb2]: Brinewake's main port city, built around a tidal lighthouse.\n  - MEMBER_OF → Lantern Guild (guild) [ID: a4140448-57b9-47e2-9fad-b44a4a957bdd]: Maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners. It does not own the mines. During winter, when the strait freezes, the guild uses stored salt. The guild opposes the toll on blue salt shipments imposed in 319.\n  - POSSESSES → Small brass key (key, item) [ID: b21607b8-9ea1-4eb5-bfad-67f4d24554c8]: A small brass key sewn inside Asha Pell's left coat cuff. It opens the old lens room beneath Vesper's lighthouse.\n  - BORN_IN → Orin (island) [ID: 31795bd3-db8b-4121-a619-b483ad06b17a]: An island where blue salt is mined by its miners.\n\nNightjar (ship, courier ship) [ID: 36eac936-9ce0-4b27-9bf4-f77ae290dfa1]: A courier ship captained by Asha Pell. It carries blue salt from Orin to Vesper only between April and September.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← CAPTAINS from Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell was born on Orin and moved to Vesper at age six, where she grew up. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - ← NAVIGATES from Iven Marr (person) [ID: 1b66c764-9ef7-438c-afa7-22338885a61e]: Asha Pell's navigator and the only person who knows she has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates the Nightjar using tide charts, not magic.\n  - CARRIES → Blue salt (mineral, resource) [ID: a904844d-81e0-40dd-9f91-77fbdc115adb]: Salt used to power the lenses of Vesper's lighthouse; mined on the island of Orin.\n\nIven Marr (person) [ID: 1b66c764-9ef7-438c-afa7-22338885a61e]: Asha Pell's navigator and the only person who knows she has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates the Nightjar using tide charts, not magic.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - NAVIGATOR_FOR → Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell was born on Orin and moved to Vesper at age six, where she grew up. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - KNOWS_ABOUT → Small brass key (key, item) [ID: b21607b8-9ea1-4eb5-bfad-67f4d24554c8]: A small brass key sewn inside Asha Pell's left coat cuff. It opens the old lens room beneath Vesper's lighthouse.\n  - NAVIGATES → Nightjar (ship, courier ship) [ID: 36eac936-9ce0-4b27-9bf4-f77ae290dfa1]: A courier ship captained by Asha Pell. It carries blue salt from Orin to Vesper only between April and September.\n\nBren Vale (person) [ID: 3866be6c-f8eb-4158-8abb-a95e3ddc64b2] [Aliases: Captain]: Bren Vale captains the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock also call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild; he refuses to join because he distrusts Tal Ren's friends. He supports the toll on blue salt shipments imposed in 319 because its revenue will repair fishing piers. Nessa is his older sister and the Petrel's cook, not his employee on a formal wage.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← OLDER_SISTER_OF from Nessa (person) [ID: d6b40b39-0aa2-4423-997e-0df62bff07c7]: Nessa is Bren Vale's older sister and the cook aboard the fishing boat Petrel. She is not Bren's employee on a formal wage. She keeps a black cat called Button aboard.\n  - CAPTAINS → Petrel (boat, fishing boat) [ID: 3f555d2a-f6ee-476b-93e5-79e9ae67c110]: A fishing boat captained by Bren Vale, with his older sister Nessa as its cook. Nessa keeps a black cat called Button aboard.\n  - UNRELATED_TO → Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell was born on Orin and moved to Vesper at age six, where she grew up. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - NOT_MEMBER_OF → Lantern Guild (guild) [ID: a4140448-57b9-47e2-9fad-b44a4a957bdd]: Maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners. It does not own the mines. During winter, when the strait freezes, the guild uses stored salt. The guild opposes the toll on blue salt shipments imposed in 319.\n  - SUPPORTS → Blue salt shipment toll (toll, policy) [ID: 08e37e67-40fc-4b69-812f-82226ba1d12b]: A toll on blue salt shipments imposed in 319 by Vesper's governor, Tal Ren. Its revenue is intended to repair fishing piers. The Lantern Guild opposes it; Bren Vale supports it because the revenue repairs fishing piers.\n\nSmall brass key (key, item) [ID: b21607b8-9ea1-4eb5-bfad-67f4d24554c8]: A small brass key sewn inside Asha Pell's left coat cuff. It opens the old lens room beneath Vesper's lighthouse.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a18769-1953-7785-bf1a-1d436775cbaf\n  - ← POSSESSES from Asha Pell (person) [ID: 5affd0ca-9c42-4463-bed7-ad12e3c38d62] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Asha Pell was born on Orin and moved to Vesper at age six, where she grew up. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - ← KNOWS_ABOUT from Iven Marr (person) [ID: 1b66c764-9ef7-438c-afa7-22338885a61e]: Asha Pell's navigator and the only person who knows she has a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates the Nightjar using tide charts, not magic.\n  - OPENS → Old lens room (ro